{"cluster_id": "C-3834", "topic": "Every positive CAS scenario in the S01-S35 suite must satisfy", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-052"], "canonical_claim": "Every positive CAS scenario in the S01-S35 suite must satisfy: SQL correctness (all replicas match the scenario oracle's aggregates), storage correctness (`ca-fsck --detail` reports `dangling = 0`), GC safety (`ca-gc-dryrun` delete candidates are a subset of the `ca-fsck` unreachable set at quiescence), a clean event audit (`system.content_addressed_log` has no error-class event types), no `Failed` GC-round finish rows, no unbounded leftovers after forced GC, and no excessive resource growth beyond the scenario budget.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/08-testing-and-soak.md#L444-L459"]}
