{"cluster_id": "C-3836", "topic": "`SYSTEM ", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-271"], "canonical_claim": "`SYSTEM ... GC` reuses the scheduler's existing `Gc` instance (a per-call one-shot would acquire the lease once then back off forever, since the steal protocol needs a stable gc_id); only the log record's Trigger differs (Manual vs scheduled). `SYSTEM ... GC REBUILD [FORCE]` instead constructs a one-shot `Gc` and calls `rebuildBaseline`, which recomputes the in-degree snapshot from raw owner state, mints numbering above every surviving ack, publishes a fresh seal, and CASes gc/state \u2014 it is live-conservative, fail-closed on refusals, and never deletes content.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/03-gc-refs.md#h-system-content-addressed-gc-manual-confirmed"]}
